{"iter": 0, "slug": "baseline", "ts": "2026-05-17T13:14:59.973706Z", "status": "kept", "family": "baseline", "composite": 0.8098, "composite_delta": 0.0, "sub_scores": {"entity_recall": 0.6764, "entity_grounding": 0.9606, "length_band": 0.6739, "decision_retention": 1.0}, "training": {}, "regressions": [], "headroom_used": 0.0, "headroom_remaining": 0.1901, "notes": "Baseline 0.7279. Target=entity_recall (owns 47% of 0.272 headroom). 4B drops ~32% of operational entities; secondary lift available on decision_retention (30%) and length_band (18%). (re-scored with corrected decision_retention rubric)"}
{"iter": 1, "slug": "h1-r16-6ep", "ts": "2026-05-17T13:34:59.872428Z", "status": "kept", "family": "H1", "target_sub_score": "entity_recall", "hypothesis": "Proven recipe lifts entity_recall by \u22655pp and composite by \u22652.5pp.", "verdict": "? Inconclusive \u2014 composite +3.17pp (meets \u22652.5pp claim) but target entity_recall was flat (-0.39pp). Lift came from length_band (+29.7pp), a confound. decision_retention regressed -10.8pp (saturated at baseline). 95% skip rate, 8 effective steps; LoRA learned 'compress more' not 'include entities'.", "composite": 0.8415, "composite_delta": 0.0317, "headroom_used": 0.167, "sub_scores": {"entity_recall": 0.6725, "entity_grounding": 0.9773, "length_band": 0.9708, "decision_retention": 0.8916}, "regressions": [{"sub_score": "decision_retention", "delta": -0.1084, "severity": "major"}, {"sub_score": "entity_recall", "delta": -0.0039, "severity": "minor"}], "training": {"rank": 16, "alpha": 32, "lr": 0.0001, "epochs": 6, "samples_per_prompt": 1, "max_tokens": 128, "top_k": 8, "effective_steps": 8, "nominal_steps": 156, "skip_rate": 0.949, "elapsed_s": 426}, "asi": {"what_worked": "Composite up +3.17pp and the lift is reproducible \u2014 length_band swap dominates. entity_grounding also improved slightly (+1.67pp) suggesting OPD does reduce hallucination at the margin.", "what_failed": "Target sub-score didn't move. Adapter learned the wrong shortcut \u2014 being shorter is easier than being more entity-complete. decision_retention regressed because the model now compresses past the decision-token threshold.", "next_focus": "Iter 2: H8 (prompt pruning) \u2014 drop prompts where the 4B already produces length-band-compliant compactions, so gradient lands on entity-recall failures. Alternative: stop here and pivot to capability #4 since the skill is producing a clear (if confounded) +3% signal even with the unfixed trainer."}, "kiln_polish_noted": true, "git_sha": "d61694e5", "notes": "95% skip rate. Pyrrhic-flavored keep: composite moved, but target sub-score didn't. Strong evidence that the unfixed trainer + short rollouts \u2192 adapter learns length compression as the lowest-cost loss reduction."}
{"iter": 2, "slug": "h1-r16-6ep-tok256", "ts": "2026-05-17T13:53:37.110578Z", "status": "kept", "family": "H1", "target_sub_score": "entity_recall", "hypothesis": "Doubling rollout max_tokens (128\u2192256) lifts entity_recall \u22653pp without losing composite gain from iter 1; iter 1's confound was that 128-tok rollout budget had no room for entity inclusion.", "verdict": "\u2713 Confirmed \u2014 entity_recall +3.46pp (0.6764\u21920.7110, claim \u2265+3pp). Composite +5.34pp vs baseline, +2.17pp vs iter 1. Lift landed on target this time (not length confound). decision_retention regression -6.14pp smaller than iter 1's -10.84pp.", "composite": 0.8632, "composite_delta": 0.0534, "headroom_used": 0.281, "sub_scores": {"entity_recall": 0.711, "entity_grounding": 0.9859, "length_band": 0.9483, "decision_retention": 0.9386}, "regressions": [{"sub_score": "decision_retention", "delta": -0.0614, "severity": "minor"}], "training": {"rank": 16, "alpha": 32, "lr": 0.0001, "epochs": 6, "samples_per_prompt": 1, "max_tokens": 256, "top_k": 8, "effective_steps": 7, "nominal_steps": 156, "skip_rate": 0.955, "elapsed_s": 504}, "asi": {"what_worked": "Max_tokens doubled and the entity_recall target moved as predicted (+3.85pp from iter 1). Diagnosis was right: with 128-tok rollouts the OPD loss collapsed onto length compression; longer rollouts gave entity inclusion somewhere to land. Inspection of 3 non-eval responses shows compactions are entity-dense (file paths, commit shas, function names) and short (29-61 words).", "what_failed": "Skip rate still 95.5% (7 effective of 156 nominal). The fundamental rollout-skip issue from capability #2 persists at this prompt set scale. decision_retention still regresses (was 1.0 at baseline; saturated \u2192 any change is a loss).", "next_focus": "Iter 3: H1-bump epochs 6\u219212 at max_tokens=256 to test if entity_recall keeps climbing. If entity_recall \u0394 vs iter 2 < +1pp, curve plateaued \u2014 pivot to H2 (more prompts) or close at iter 2 (28% headroom captured)."}, "kiln_polish_noted": true, "git_sha": "46b8e6e5", "notes": "BEST RESULT YET on this capability. Three iters in, target sub-score moved as predicted by mechanism. The rollout-max_tokens knob is now a known important lever \u2014 needs to be wider than the natural response length so OPD has room to learn content rather than length."}
